meta {
  name: Request Withdrawal
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/counsellor/wallet/withdraw
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "amount": 1000
  }
}

docs {
  Submits a withdrawal request. The wallet balance is NOT decremented at
  this point — the transaction is created with withdrawal_status =
  "pending" and the balance is only debited once a super admin approves it
  (PATCH /api/v1/admin/counsellors/withdrawals/:id/status). If rejected,
  no wallet change ever happens since nothing was debited.
  Requires: counsellor access token (academic counsellors only).

  Validation:
  - amount must be ≤ "available" balance, i.e. current wallet balance
    minus the total of all of this counsellor's other pending withdrawal
    requests (prevents overcommitting funds across multiple pending
    requests since none of them have actually debited the balance yet)
  - amount must be ≥ platform config `counsellorMinWithdrawalAmount`
    (see GET /api/v1/admin/config)
  - the counsellor's profile must have upi_id and/or bank_details set
    (PATCH /api/v1/counsellor/profile) — otherwise 400
    "Add a UPI ID or bank details to your profile before requesting a
    withdrawal"

  Payout details are no longer sent per-request — they're read from the
  counsellor's profile and snapshotted onto the transaction (UPI preferred
  if both are set) so later profile edits don't change past requests.

  Response: { transaction_id, amount, withdrawal_status, balance_after }
  balance_after reflects the unchanged wallet balance at request time —
  it only drops once the request is approved.

  Tables: counsellor_wallets, counsellor_wallet_transactions, counsellors
}
